@{
    
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

<style>
    body {
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    .bg-welfare-left {
        background-color: #0747AE;
        padding: 15px;
    }

        .bg-welfare-left h3 {
            font-size: 21px;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: #fff;
        }

        .bg-welfare-left ul li {
            margin-top: 18px;
            font-size: 17px;
            color: #fff;
        }

            .bg-welfare-left ul li a {
                color: #fff;
                text-decoration: none;
            }

                .bg-welfare-left ul li a:hover {
                    text-decoration: underline;
                }   

    .content-box {
        border: 1px dashed #000;
        background: #fff;
        padding: 20px;
    }

    .welfare-font {
        font-size: 17px;
        color: #000;
        text-align: justify;
        line-height: 1.8;
    }

    hr {
        border: 1px solid #000;
    }
</style>

<!-- ================= BANNER ================= -->
<div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-12 p-0" style="margin-top:-20px;
        background:url('https://img.freepik.com/premium-photo/extensive-collection-books-library_868797-8212.jpg') center/cover fixed;">
        <div style="background:rgba(0,0,0,0.5)">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="d-flex flex-column justify-content-center" style="min-height:300px;">
                    <h3 class="display-6 text-white fw-bold">
                        Department of Civil Engineering
                    </h3>
                    <div class="d-inline-flex text-white">
                        <a href="/" class="text-white text-decoration-none">Home</a>
                        <i class="fa fa-angle-double-right px-2 pt-1"></i>
                        <span>Department of Civil Engineering</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ================= MAIN CONTENT ================= -->
<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="row">
        <style>
            .bg-welfare-left ul li {
                margin-top: 20px;
                font-size: 17px;
                line-height: 1.5;
                color: #fff;
                font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            }

            .bg-welfare-left hr {
                border-bottom: 2px solid white !important;
            }
        </style>
                @Html.Partial("~/Views/Shared/DeptSidebar/_CVLE_Sidebar.cshtml")

        <!-- RIGHT CONTENT -->
        <div class="col-lg-9">
            <div class="content-box">

                <h2 class="fw-bold" style="color:#0747AE;">About</h2>
                <hr />
                <p class="welfare-font" style="margin-top:10px;">
                    The BTech program in civil engineering offers a comprehensive education in the planning, design, construction and maintenance of infrastructure essential to modern society. The core curriculum encompasses key areas, including Structural Engineering, Geotechnical Engineering, Transportation Engineering, Water Resources Engineering, Environmental Engineering, and Construction Technology and Management.
                    Students gain both theoretical understanding and hands-on experience through laboratory work, design projects, and field training. With the growing need for innovative, sustainable, and resilient infrastructure, the program integrates emerging topics like Sustainable Construction Practices, Environmental Impact Assessment, Smart City Planning, Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS), and Climate-Responsive Infrastructure. Students are also introduced to advanced tools and technologies, including Building Information Modelling (BIM), Geographic Information Systems (GIS), Remote Sensing, and Construction Automation. Students benefit from modern laboratories, advanced software tools, field surveys, and hands-on training that enhance their technical competence and problem-solving abilities. This blend of traditional knowledge and modern innovation equips graduates to address global challenges in urbanization, climate change, and resource management, preparing them for impactful careers in public infrastructure, urban development, consultancy, and research.
                    With a focus on producing competent, ethical, and industry-ready engineers, the Department of Civil Engineering strives to make meaningful contributions to nation-building and the development of more intelligent, safer, and more resilient infrastructure.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
































